G5007.def:
τάλαντομ, -ον, τ 
[in LXX for כִּכָּר ;] 
__1. a balance (Hom.). 
__2. that which is weighed, a talent; 
__(a) a talent in weight (in Horn. always of gold); 
__(b) a sum of money, whether gold or silver, equivalent to a talent in weight (see DB, iii, 418 ff.): Matthieu 18:24 25:15 ff.†

G5043.def:
τέκνον, -ου, τό 
(τίκτω), [in LXX chiefly for בֵּן, also for יֶלֶד, etc. ;] 
that which is begotten, born (cf. Scottish bairn), a child of either sex: Marc 13:12, Luc 1:7, Actes 7:5; pl., Matthieu 7:11, Marc 7:27, Luc 1:17, Éphésiens 6:1, al.; τέκνα ἐπαγγελίας, Romains 9:8; τ. τῆς σαρκός, ib.; in a wider sense (as Heb. בָּנִים), of posterity, Matthieu 2:18, Luc 3:8, al.; specif., of a male child, Matthieu 21:28, Actes 21:21, a,l.; in voc. as a form of kindly address from an elder to a junior or from a teacher to a disciple, Matthieu 9:2 21:28, Marc 2:5, Luc 2:48; τ. μου (= cl. τ. μοι; see Bl., §37, 5), Galates 4:19 (τεκνία, WH, txt.), 2 Timothée 2:1. Metaphorical, 
__(a) of disciples (apart from direct address, see supr.): Phm 10, 1 Timothée 1:2, Tite 1:4, 3Jo.4; 
__(b) with reference to the Fatherhood of God (see: πατήρ, γεννάω), τέκνα τ. θεοῦ (cf. Ésaïe 30:1, Wis.16:21): Romains 8:16, Éphésiens 5:1, Philippiens 2:15; and esp. in Johannine bks. (cf. Westc, Epp. Jo., 94, 120), Jean 1:12, 1 Jean 3:1 al.; 
__(with) of those who imitate others and are therefore regarded as the spiritual offspring of their exemplars: Matthieu 3:9, Luc 3:8, Jean 8:39, Romains 9:7, 1 Pierre 3:6; τ. διαβόλου, 1 Jean 3:10; 
__(d) as in Heb. (LXX, Joël 2:23, Psaumes 149:2, 1Ma.1:38), of the inhabitants of a city: Matthieu 23:37, Luc 13:34 19:44, Galates 4:25; 
__(e) with an adjectival genitive, frequently rendering a Heb. expression, adopted from LXX or formed on the analogy of its language, but sometimes with parallels in Gk. writers (see Deiss., BS, 161ff.): τέκνα φωτός, Éphésiens 5:8; τ. ὑπακοῆς, 1 Pierre 1:14; κατάρας, 2 Pierre 2:14; ὀργῆς, Éphésiens 2:3. 
SYN.: see: παῖς.
